-- Weapon (Launcher) module entries (plan.md §2.8). The second weapon
-- subtype alongside Auto Cannons: unlike a cannon, a launcher never fires
-- on its own - it launches a missile or torpedo consumed from
-- `main/data/ordinance.lua`, and carries no damage/range stats of its own
-- (that lives on the ordinance it fires).
--
-- Two subtypes, per §2.8's decision:
--   general          - a general-purpose missile launcher; fires missiles,
--                      which are broadly interchangeable across launchers.
--   nuclear_launcher - fires NUCLEAR TORPEDOES ONLY. A nuclear torpedo is
--                      restricted to this subtype and cannot be loaded into
--                      a general launcher (§2.8's compatibility rule; §2.6
--                      gates it behind Valour).
-- `launcher_type` is the local field holding this subtype, and is what an
-- ordinance entry's own `compatible_weapon` must match to be loadable -
-- "general" here pairs with `compatible_weapon = "general"` missiles, and
-- "nuclear_launcher" with the `nuclear_launcher` torpedo. Enforced by
-- data, not by separate tables per weapon (§2.8).
--
-- Naming (decided, revised - "exact reference names", per direct
-- instruction): launchers now carry the reference game's OWN published
-- designations verbatim where it has them (bsgo.fandom.com/wiki/Weapons) -
